WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:04.904
-Hey, guys. Welcome back to "The
Tonight Show: At Home Edition."

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.205
My name is Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:06.205 --> 00:00:08.007
I want to thank you guys so much
for watching our show.

00:00:08.007 --> 00:00:10.309
And we've gotten
such amazing feedback

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:13.312
from around -- not just
the country, but the world.

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:15.447
And so it really means
a lot to us

00:00:15.447 --> 00:00:17.850
that you're choosing to watch us
to -- to make you laugh

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.786
and kind of give you a little
ease in the tense times.

00:00:20.786 --> 00:00:22.655
Thank you very, very much.

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.356
We definitely got some --
some notice

00:00:24.356 --> 00:00:25.791
from a couple corporations

00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:28.128
that wanted to help us out
in raising money.

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:29.529
So I really want to thank --

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:33.099
State Farm is willing to --

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:35.168
Get ready for this, guys.
This is big news.

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:38.805
They're going to match
up to $100,000,

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:41.374
with all the money
going to Red Cross.

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:43.576
They're going to match this week
up to a hun--

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:46.045
that's $200,000 we can raise
this week.

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:48.014
So please donate
to right here --

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:51.016
redcross.org/statefarm.

00:00:51.016 --> 00:00:52.484
Thank you, thank you, thank you

00:00:52.484 --> 00:00:55.088
to our neighbors at State Farm
for doing that.

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:56.356
That means a lot to us,

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:58.290
and we'll be talking about this
this whole week

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.393
on our show tonight.

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:05.131
I hope everyone
who stayed at home had a --

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.399
Oh, hi, buddy.
Nice to see you.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.434
We -- You can show what we did,
Frannie, right?

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:10.436
What did we do over the weekend?

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:12.739
Can we...?
We -- No, we --

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.340
we colored this in, didn't we?
-Yes.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.976
-Now, Winnie,
did you color any of this?

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:18.110
-Yeah.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:22.081
-This is our
market stand/lemonade stand

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:24.451
that took us four days to do.

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:26.619
I was just --
look at these colors.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.254
I mean, are you kidding me?

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:32.458
And so I thought
what would be fun is that

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:34.260
we could use it as --
almost like a desk,

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.628
like Daddy's desk at work,

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:37.397
and I could read you some jokes.

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:38.631
Do you guys want to hear
some jokes?

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:39.765
-No. [ Laughs ]

00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:41.501
-We have
an amazing show tonight.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.402
Kim Kardashian West is my guest.

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:44.704
We'll be Zooming with her,

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.973
talking about her new
documentary airing on Oxygen

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:49.242
about criminal justice reform

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:51.911
and, also, all the money
she's giving

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:53.879
through her company SKIMS
to charity,

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:56.549
which is really awesome
that she's doing that.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:59.885
Then we're gonna talk to
music superstar Jon Bon Jovi,

00:01:59.885 --> 00:02:04.790
who is doing amazing stuff
with JBJSoulKitchen.org --

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:07.560
that is his charity
that he's talking about today.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.362
We'll be talking to Jon
about that

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:13.799
and, also, his new song that
you can sing with him through.

00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:15.568
You'll see later in the show.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:17.903
Then we have great music
from OneRepublic.

00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:19.705
I'm so happy
you guys did that for us.

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:21.307
Thank you so much, OneRepublic.

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:25.178
Brand-new song from them
from their home.

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:26.545
I thought
it would be kind of cool

00:02:26.545 --> 00:02:30.049
to do some monologue jokes now,
so let's get going.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.951
Here we go.

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:34.187
Welcome to "The Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.254
Let's get to some news.

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:36.789
Well, guys,
in these crazy times,

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:38.758
Taco Bell announced that,
tomorrow,

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:42.261
they're offering every American
one free Doritos Locos Taco.

00:02:42.261 --> 00:02:43.796
Experts are calling it

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:47.000
"not what we need during a
national toilet paper shortage."

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.170
[ Fireplace hissing softly ]

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:55.241
Love the nice hiss
of the gas fireplace.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:57.042
[ Fireplace hissing softly ]

00:02:57.042 --> 00:02:58.744
Meanwhile, over in Moscow,

00:02:58.744 --> 00:03:00.746
a citywide quarantine
has been imposed

00:03:00.746 --> 00:03:04.583
where everyone will be trapped
by a smart monitoring system,

00:03:04.583 --> 00:03:06.852
and residents will need
permission to leave their homes,

00:03:06.852 --> 00:03:11.256
or, as that's known in Russia,
Monday.

00:03:11.256 --> 00:03:13.192
Some sports news --
the Wimbledon tennis tournament

00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:15.762
is the next big sporting event
that will be canceled.

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:17.496
Don't worry --
if you still want to hear

00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:19.165
men and women grunting all day,

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:22.835
just listen to the quarantined
couple next door who won't stop.

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:25.338
Earmuffs, you know.

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:26.805
Some business news --
as of Friday,

00:03:26.805 --> 00:03:28.207
the videoconferencing
company Zoom

00:03:28.207 --> 00:03:31.277
has valued
at more than $40 billion,

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:33.312
or roughly as much as Uber,

00:03:33.312 --> 00:03:35.281
which makes sense,
since they're both places

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:37.684
where users have no idea
how to mute themselves.

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:40.620
Listen to this --
I heard that a lot of people

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.055
are doing virtual sessions
with their therapists,

00:03:43.055 --> 00:03:44.456
but it's hard
because they can't talk

00:03:44.456 --> 00:03:46.426
about their significant others.

00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:48.293
When the doctor says,
"How's your relationship?"

00:03:48.293 --> 00:03:51.497
you have to go,
"It's very good."

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:55.401
I saw that some people
have been posting

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:58.137
throwback photos of themselves
online.

00:03:58.137 --> 00:03:59.572
Gets awkward when you comment,

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.407
"Wow, you looked
so young back then,"

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:03.476
and they're like,
"That was from two weeks ago."

00:04:05.544 --> 00:04:07.913
This isn't good --
last night, a Dutch museum says

00:04:07.913 --> 00:04:10.249
that a Vincent Van Gogh painting
was stolen.

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:12.685
Apparently, the security guard
tried stopping the thieves,

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:15.321
but he couldn't
get within six feet of them.

00:04:16.388 --> 00:04:17.957
[ Rhythmic tapping ]

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:20.860
Listen to this --
according to a new study,

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:22.595
the majority
of medical marijuana

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:27.099
is stronger than it needs to be
for pain relief purposes.

00:04:27.099 --> 00:04:28.434
You can read more
about the study

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:31.437
in the "Journal
of American Narc Physicians."

00:04:33.138 --> 00:04:35.808
And finally, the movie
"Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles"

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:38.678
hit theaters 30 years ago today.

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:40.746
They all wore masks,
ate lots of pizza,

00:04:40.746 --> 00:04:42.115
and were hidden away
from society.

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:45.117
So, basically,
we're all Ninja Turtles now.

00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:46.419
Thank you very much.

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:48.887
That's our monologue
right there, everybody.

00:04:48.887 --> 00:04:51.524
Hey, we want to check in
on our very good friend,

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:52.758
one of my best friends.

00:04:52.758 --> 00:04:54.727
You know him -- you love him --
Steve Higgins.

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:56.262
So I got to check in on him
today.

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:57.330
He's doing great.

00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:00.265
Here's Steve at home
with his family.

00:05:00.265 --> 00:05:01.501
Higgins!

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.168
-Hey!
How's it going, man?

00:05:03.168 --> 00:05:04.637
-Hey. I missed your face, dude.

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:06.038
How you doing, buddy?
You look great.

00:05:06.038 --> 00:05:07.706
-Oh, so good.
Everything's good.

00:05:07.706 --> 00:05:09.741
Everything's as good as can be.

00:05:09.741 --> 00:05:11.644
-Where are you now?
Where -- Where exactly are you?

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:14.247
-We're -- We're at the house --
the boys and I and Ellen.

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:15.715
We're staying at the house.

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:19.285
And Anna's staying in the city,
nursing at Mount Sinai West.

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:20.820
-Oh, my.
-God bless her.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:22.588
-How is she doing?
I love Anna so much.

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:24.056
I'm so proud of her, dude.

00:05:24.056 --> 00:05:25.658
-She is thank-- She's just --

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:27.460
She says she's just exhausted
every night.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:30.029
So she just comes home
and goes to sleep, goes back --

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:32.231
[Chuckling]
wakes up, goes back into work,

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:33.499
and she's on the front line,
so...

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:35.634
-She's on the front lines
for us, fighting for us.

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:37.070
Tell her I'm so proud of her,
please,

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:38.237
and give her my best...
-Oh, I will.

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:39.338
-...'cause I knew her when --

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:40.773
I used to call her
"Anna Banana."

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:42.407
She was 5 when I --
-Yeah.

00:05:42.407 --> 00:05:43.876
[ Chuckling ] Exactly.

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:45.378
I mean, you did meet her
when she was 5 years old.

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:46.813
How crazy is that?

00:05:46.813 --> 00:05:50.049
-And -- And you have your --
Are your sons there, as well?

00:05:50.049 --> 00:05:51.517
-Yep,
all three of them are here.

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:53.853
And then Ellen's here, and we're
just at the -- at the house,

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:56.589
trying to kind of --
just staying quarantined.

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:58.223
But I tell you,
watching you and Frannie

00:05:58.223 --> 00:06:00.058
has really made me --
it's made all our days.

00:06:00.058 --> 00:06:01.627
It's so fun.
-Oh, dude --

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:03.229
-Just watching her climb --
climb all over you.

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:05.631
[ Both laugh ]
-Yeah. No, there's no rules.

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:07.433
I mean, they're -- they're kids,
so the kids are gonna be kids.

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:08.401
-Dad!
-Okay, bud.

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:09.635
-Dad!

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:10.769
-Just let me talk to Jimmy
for a second. Okay.

00:06:10.769 --> 00:06:12.004
-Dad?
-Alright, alright.

00:06:12.004 --> 00:06:14.006
-What?
-[ Chuckling ] Okay.

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:16.642
Alrighty. Okay.
Alright.

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:18.010
[ Laughter ]
-Dad?

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:20.813
-Got him! Got him!
-Dad!

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:23.015
-Alright.
-Mom!

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:25.451
-Alright.
-Oh, bunny ears.

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:26.886
[ Chuckles ]
-Alright.

00:06:26.886 --> 00:06:30.122
-Stop! Ohh!
-[ Laughing ] Okay.

00:06:30.122 --> 00:06:31.590
-Oh. Uh, say, guys --

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:34.493
-Okay, okay, everybody back.
Get back there.

00:06:34.493 --> 00:06:35.861
Ohh!

00:06:35.861 --> 00:06:37.696
-Alright, okay.

00:06:37.696 --> 00:06:39.932
-I'm gonna let you go.
I'm gonna let you go, okay, bud?

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:41.266
-Ohh!
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.266 --> 00:06:43.235
-Take care. Um, I'll talk you
to later on, alright?

00:06:43.235 --> 00:06:44.737
I'll -- I'll text you.

